const e="fls3n-indonesia-student-arts-literature",h=2025,t="Translated from Indonesian and read in full (printed pages i to 64, plus the two appendix letters). Captured: purpose, themes, eligibility and letters, school, regency/city and national selection, upload rules, the full 2025 schedule, awards and SIMT recording, jury rules, sanctions and complaints, and every rule and criteria table of the 7 branches. A newer 2026 FLS3N SD guide exists (summaries on education sites) but no official 2026 document was found, so the 2025 official guide is used and its dates are the 2025 edition. Placing points are not printed. The guide's own Storytelling heading says SMP/MTs; the content is for primary school. The Craft criteria table prints weights 25/25/20/20/10 and 1 to 10 scales; the Expressive Drawing guide prints a score range of 100 to 1000. Two national themes are printed for the drawing branch (preliminary and final). The Dance resolution is printed as 750p. The guide prints the Pantomime music folder as a Google Drive link, listed under Documents. No bank, home or personal data are printed.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"FLS3N 2025, primary school (SD/MI) level. Festival Lomba Seni dan Sastra Siswa Nasional (National Student Arts and Literature Festival and Competition).","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The school operator registers the students on the BPTI registration portal from {{RegistrationOpen}} until {{RegistrationClose}}. The national final is online on {{NationalFinalDates}}. Only students in class 3, 4 or 5 can take part, and each school can enter at most 2 students or teams in one branch. Each regency or city sends its single best entry in each branch to the national preliminary round.","Notes":["The theme of FLS3N 2025 is {{GeneralTheme}}. The special theme is {{SpecialTheme}}.","Seven branches are held for primary school: Expressive Drawing, Solo Singing, Craft, Storytelling, Story Writing, Pantomime (2 performers) and Dance (3 to 5 performers).","The national preliminary round and the national final are both held online.","Works are sent as video or digital documents through a Google Drive or YouTube link. Test the link before you send it.","The schedule can change. Changes are announced on the official BPTI and Pusat Prestasi Nasional websites."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["FLS3N gives students a place to explore, develop and show their arts talent. It is a way to grow love for arts and culture and to build creative, high-achieving and competitive young people.","The festival is held by the Balai Pengembangan Talenta Indonesia (BPTI, Indonesian Talent Development Centre), Pusat Prestasi Nasional (National Achievement Centre), Ministry of Primary and Secondary Education.","The Ministry has held a national arts talent event for students since 2008. In 2025 the event grew from FLS2N into FLS3N (with literature) and the national level is held online.","FLS3N 2025 has 47 branches in total: 15 for primary education, 15 for secondary education and 17 for students with special needs. This guide covers the 7 primary school (SD/MI/equivalent) branches.","The general theme of FLS3N 2025 is {{GeneralTheme}}.","The special theme is {{SpecialTheme}}: wake up early, worship, exercise, eat healthy and nutritious food, love learning, take part in society, and sleep early.","Performing arts (pertunjukan) are shown through movement, sound or expression in front of an audience. The material can be prepared at regency/city or province level following this guide.","Creation arts (penciptaan) focus on a lasting work such as a drawing, craft or literary work. Knowledge, materials and tools are prepared by the participant at regency/city or province level, following the themes in the guide.","Selection runs in steps: school, then regency or city (and province), then the national level, which has a preliminary round and a final round.","A regency or city Education Office can hold its selection online or offline, for all branches or only some, depending on geography, funding and resources. Its own rules follow this guide.","The copyright of a competition work stays with the participant.","The right to copy, reproduce, distribute or convert national-level works, in part or whole, for non-commercial use belongs to BPTI.","Everything in the guide may change as conditions and policy change. BPTI announces a change as soon as it is decided, through a separate document or other channel."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["The participant is an Indonesian citizen (WNI) in Indonesia, or a student of an Indonesian School Overseas (SILN), and is registered as an active student.","The school is an accredited school in Indonesia, or a school overseas recognised by the Ministry.","The participant is an active primary school student (SD/MI or equivalent).","At registration the student is in class 3, 4 or 5.","The student has a valid national student number (NISN) and a valid national identity number (NIK).","The student is synchronised in the national education data systems Dapodik and PD Data.","Each school can register a maximum of 2 participants or teams in the same branch.","The student has not been Juara 1, 2 or 3 at national level in FLS2N, LS2N or AKA PDBK in the same branch and level in the previous year.","The participant signs a Statement of Originality of the Work (Surat Pernyataan Keaslian Karya) with a Rp10,000 stamp, and the Principal signs a Statement of Document Accuracy (Surat Keterangan Kebenaran Dokumen) with a Rp10,000 stamp. Both are saved as one PDF file and uploaded to the FLS3N application system. Examples are in the guide appendix.","The participant's statement says: the student registered is the participant, the work is the participant's own original work, the participant is fully responsible for any copying that breaks copyright, and the participant accepts any decision of the jury and committee if dishonesty is found.","The Principal's statement says: the student is still active, all uploaded documents are correct and match the student, and the student has not been Juara 1, 2 or 3 in AKA-PDBK, LS2N or FLS2N SD/MI at national level in the same branch and level."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Step 1, school selection: the school finds, selects and decides its best representative in each branch. The school operator registers the student on the BPTI registration portal ({{RegistrationPortal}}).","The school sends its students to the regency or city selection.","Step 2, regency or city selection: the regency or city Education Office uses the data of the students registered on the portal. It picks 1 best participant or team in each branch.","If the Juara 1 cannot take part, Juara 2 can take the place, and so on. A student who did not come through the regency or city selection cannot take the place.","The winners are fixed by a decision letter (SK) of the Head of the regency or city Education Office, and they win the right to join the national preliminary round.","The SK, video and digital documents of the winners are sent to BPTI Puspresnas through the FLS3N SD/MI application system.","A regency or city online selection uses the same registered student data. Its rules and process are set by each Education Office, following this guide.","The national preliminary round is online. One participant or team from each regency or city enters each branch.","BPTI groups the works by province, judges them, and decides the winners of each province: Juara 1, 2, 3 and Juara Harapan 1, 2, 3, in a decision letter.","Juara 1 of each province goes to the national final. If Juara 1 cannot take part, Juara 2 can take the place, and so on. A person who is not a preliminary round result cannot take the place.","The national final is online. The participants are all Juara 1 of the preliminary round in each branch (the National Finalists).","Digital work upload rules: the work is a video or digital document as set by each branch.","Video is MP4 with at least 720p resolution. Text documents are PDF. A photo or scan of a picture is PDF at 300 dpi.","Name each file in the format set in the branch rules.","Before upload, put all the files in one folder named Province_Participant Name_Branch_FLS3N SD 2025 (the name can change as the branch rules say).","Upload the folder to the participant's own Google Drive and set access to Anyone with the link can view, so the committee and jury can open it.","A video can also go to the participant's YouTube account, set to unlisted, and the YouTube link is uploaded to the application system.","The participant must enter the Google Drive or YouTube link in the FLS3N SD/MI application system.","Test the link first. The participant is responsible for the link and its files being valid and complete until the results are announced.","Upload before the date and time set in the schedule. The system closes upload after the deadline.","After the link is uploaded, the participant gets a notification that the upload was received.","The application system is used for registration, participant data, marking regency or city winners, uploading works, uploading the winners' SK, downloading tutorials, national jury marking and other data. Sites: {{EventApp}}, {{InfoSites}}."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["The guide prints no entry fee for participants.","The statement letters each need a Rp10,000 stamp: {{StampFee}}.","Regional events are paid from the regional budget (APBD) or other funds under the regional authority. The national event is paid from the 2025 state budget (APBN) given to BPTI Puspresnas."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Important Dates","Items":["Introduction of FLS3N Dikdas 2025 (sosialisasi): {{Socialisation}}.","Registration through the BPTI portal and data sync to the application system (school operator): from {{RegistrationOpen}} to {{RegistrationClose}}.","Registration data for regency or city selection is sent to the regency or city Education Office on {{DistrictNotice}}.","FLS3N regency or city level, upload of the winners' SK, videos and works, and marking of winners in the application system (Education Office operator): {{DistrictRoundDates}}.","Last date for the regency or city SK, video and work upload and winner marking: {{DistrictRoundDeadline}}.","National preliminary round: participants announced on {{PreliminaryAnnouncement}}; judged by the national jury (BPTI) on {{PreliminaryJudging}}.","Results of the preliminary round, the SK of the province winners and the SK of the National Finalists are published on the Puspresnas website on {{PreliminaryResults}}.","Upload window for the National Finalists' work files (school or regency/city operator): {{FinalUploadWindow}}.","National final (online): {{NationalFinalDates}}.","The SK of the national winners is published on the Puspresnas and BPTI websites, and winners are announced on Puspresnas Instagram, on {{WinnersAnnounced}}.","If the schedule changes, an announcement letter on the official BPTI and Pusat Prestasi Nasional websites tells everyone."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Rounds and Qualification","Items":["School level: the school selects its representative (maximum 2 per branch) and registers them.","Regency or city level: one best participant or team per branch is chosen, by an online or offline selection as the Education Office decides.","National preliminary round (online): one participant or team from each regency or city in each branch. BPTI picks the winners of each province.","National final (online): Juara 1 of each province in each branch (National Finalists). The national jury picks the national winners.","The levels of the competition are school, regency or city and province, and national."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["The jury team in each branch has 1 chair judge and 2 member judges.","A regency or city jury member must have expertise in the branch, proved by a certificate, a CV, a licence or an equal recognition, and must be professional: no conflict of interest, not the coach of a participant of the same event and institution, and no record of unprofessional judging.","Regency or city judges must come from different sub-districts (kecamatan) or equal bodies. Province judges must come from different regencies or cities or equal bodies.","The choice of judges takes into account the representation of regions and interested organisations.","Judges are not from the organisers or committee of the same event.","Regency or city judges are chosen, appointed and evaluated by the authorised officer of the regency or city. National judges for each branch are chosen, appointed and evaluated by the Head of BPTI.","Marks are out of 100 in this template. Branch criteria and weights are given under each competition."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Recognition","Items":["Regency or city level: certificates or e-certificates for participants and winners are issued by the local Education Office.","Achievements at regency or city level can be recorded in the Talent Management Information System (SIMT) of Pusat Prestasi Nasional. The recorded achievements are Juara 1, 2, 3 and Juara Harapan 1, 2, 3.","Recording in SIMT gives official recognition from the Ministry, a chance of academic incentives (a possible priority in the new student admission system, SPMB) and documentation of achievements in the national talent management programme.","The regency or city Education Office operator must enter or mark the winners in the application system, based on the Education Office's winner SK. If the achievement is not recorded, the student loses these benefits.","National preliminary round: Juara 1, 2, 3 and Juara Harapan 1, 2, 3 of each province receive an e-certificate from BPTI and are recorded in SIMT by BPTI.","National final results are recorded in SIMT automatically by BPTI for Juara 1, 2, 3, Juara Harapan 1, 2, 3 and Finalists.","National final Juara 1: gold medal, e-certificate and development money (uang pembinaan).","National final Juara 2: silver medal, e-certificate and development money.","National final Juara 3: bronze medal, e-certificate and development money.","National final Juara Harapan 1, 2 and 3: e-certificate and development money.","National Finalists who are not winners (as registered on the BPTI portal) get an FLS3N participation e-certificate from BPTI.","E-certificates are downloaded at {{CertificateSite}}. One email account can be used by only one person. Use a personal email and type the address correctly."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Sanctions","Items":["Participants must follow the rules and the set schedule.","A participant's entry is cancelled if the participant: dies, withdraws, breaks the event rules, commits violence (intolerance, sexual violence or bullying), is involved in drug use or dealing, or is involved in a crime.","At national level the Head of Pusat Prestasi Nasional cancels the participation.","A win or award can be cancelled if: there is cheating in the event, the procedure or ethics of the event are broken, a crime related to intolerance, sexual violence or bullying is committed, or a serious crime related to corruption, drugs or treason is committed.","Cancellation is based on a complaint report."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints","Items":["Anyone can make a complaint report in person (spoken) or in writing through the reporting channels of BPTI Puspresnas: a written letter, telephone, a text message, email, photo, video, screenshot or another way that is easy for the reporter.","BPTI Puspresnas follows up the complaint with an investigation of the violation and the cancellation. The investigation is based on the evidence sent."]},{"Key":"reporting","Title":"Results and Reporting","Items":["The Education Office issues the SK of the regency or city winners, signed by the Head of the Education Office, and gives the winners their certificates.","The regency or city operator marks the winners in the application system and uploads the SK.","BPTI publishes the decision letters (SK) for province winners, National Finalists and national winners on its website and the Puspresnas website, where all participants can open them.","BPTI evaluates the event after it ends."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Classes of FLS3N","Items":["FLS3N 2025 also has a secondary school (SMP/MTs, SMA/SMK) set of 15 branches and a special needs (disabilitas) set of 17 branches. These have their own guides and are not part of this template."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025 (Indonesian)","Url":"https://pusatprestasinasional.kemdikbud.go.id/uploads/lampiran/Panduan%20Teknis%20Pelaksanaan%20FLS3N%20SD%202025.pdf"},{"Title":"Pantomime accompaniment music folder (BPTI)","Url":"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1oVihnc5XQ2T_6SkX6_9KAxS70baZqpbN"}]}`),a=[],i=[{AgeGroup:"SD Individual",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab II A and B; Bab III",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Active primary school (SD/MI) students in class 3, 4 or 5 at registration.","One participant per entry. This group takes Expressive Drawing, Solo Singing, Craft, Storytelling and Story Writing."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Active primary school (SD/MI) students in class 3, 4 or 5 at registration.
- One participant per entry. This group takes Expressive Drawing, Solo Singing, Craft, Storytelling and Story Writing.`},{AgeGroup:"SD Team",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab II A; Bab III F and G",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Active primary school (SD/MI) students in class 3, 4 or 5 at registration.","Pantomime is a group of 2 participants. Dance is a group of 3 to 5 participants."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Active primary school (SD/MI) students in class 3, 4 or 5 at registration.
- Pantomime is a group of 2 participants. Dance is a group of 3 to 5 participants.`}],o=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Expressive Drawing (Gambar Ekspresi)","Source":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab III A (pages 23-28)","Sections":{"About":["Expressive drawing is a drawing made freely from imagination, with the drawer's own interpretation and view, so it shows the strength of the object drawn.","Aims: to teach drawing technique, tools and materials; to strengthen imagination and interpretation so that participants think creatively; to make original work that is not copied; and to build character: independence, honesty, hard work, persistence, discipline, tolerance, solidarity, love of country and responsibility.","Stages: the regency or city competition is held by each region, and the drawing is made at a place that the region sets. In the preliminary round the Juara 1 of each regency or city sends the work through the application page, and the national jury picks one winner for each province. In the final, the best work of each province is ranked Juara 1, 2, 3 and Juara Harapan 1, 2, 3."],"TimeAndFormat":["Preliminary round theme: {{DrawingPreliminaryTheme}}. Draw an elder or younger sibling, father or mother, grandparent or someone close in the family. Show their face and figure, or show closeness, for example on holiday in the village, watching television together, walking to the rice field or watching the sea on the beach. The drawing can be close up or from far, with a focus on the face or on the figure from a distance. Draw a family moment you love.","Final round theme: {{DrawingFinalTheme}}. Draw a sport you like: riding a bicycle, running, swimming, a healthy walk and more.","Medium: a colour drawing on A3 paper, with crayon, watercolour, coloured pencil or mixed media (choose one, or mix them).","Send these files: (1) a photo or scan of the colour work as a PDF, 300 dpi, sharp and not pixelated (about 1 to 3 MB); (2) a photo of the participant holding the work, with no uniform or badge; (3) MP4 video, at least 720p, of 30 seconds each, close up, showing the tools and materials, the drawing at about 50% with the face and the whole body visible, and the drawing at 90 to 100% with the face and whole body visible.","Put the work and the process video in a folder named Penyisihan SD_Gambar Ekspresi_Regency/City Name_Participant Name_Video/Foto for the preliminary round, or Final SD_Gambar Ekspresi_Regency/City Name_Participant Name_Video/Foto for the final round. Upload to the participant's Google Drive with Anyone with the link can view, and enter the Google Drive or YouTube link in the application system."],"Rules":["Content must not carry SARA (ethnicity, religion, race and inter-group), pornography, provocative or political elements."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Weights: fit of the theme and story 10%; insight and knowledge about the chosen theme 20%; creativity (idea and handling of all visual aspects) 20%; aesthetic principles (composition, rhythm, depth or dimension, accent) 20%; skill in visual elements (shape, colour, line and plane) 20%; mastery of the drawing medium and tools 10%. Total 100%.","The mark range printed in the guide is 100 to 1000."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Expressive drawing is a drawing made freely from imagination, with the drawer's own interpretation and view, so it shows the strength of the object drawn.\\n- Aims: to teach drawing technique, tools and materials; to strengthen imagination and interpretation so that participants think creatively; to make original work that is not copied; and to build character: independence, honesty, hard work, persistence, discipline, tolerance, solidarity, love of country and responsibility.\\n- Stages: the regency or city competition is held by each region, and the drawing is made at a place that the region sets. In the preliminary round the Juara 1 of each regency or city sends the work through the application page, and the national jury picks one winner for each province. In the final, the best work of each province is ranked Juara 1, 2, 3 and Juara Harapan 1, 2, 3.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Preliminary round theme: {{DrawingPreliminaryTheme}}. Draw an elder or younger sibling, father or mother, grandparent or someone close in the family. Show their face and figure, or show closeness, for example on holiday in the village, watching television together, walking to the rice field or watching the sea on the beach. The drawing can be close up or from far, with a focus on the face or on the figure from a distance. Draw a family moment you love.\\n- Final round theme: {{DrawingFinalTheme}}. Draw a sport you like: riding a bicycle, running, swimming, a healthy walk and more.\\n- Medium: a colour drawing on A3 paper, with crayon, watercolour, coloured pencil or mixed media (choose one, or mix them).\\n- Send these files: (1) a photo or scan of the colour work as a PDF, 300 dpi, sharp and not pixelated (about 1 to 3 MB); (2) a photo of the participant holding the work, with no uniform or badge; (3) MP4 video, at least 720p, of 30 seconds each, close up, showing the tools and materials, the drawing at about 50% with the face and the whole body visible, and the drawing at 90 to 100% with the face and whole body visible.\\n- Put the work and the process video in a folder named Penyisihan SD_Gambar Ekspresi_Regency/City Name_Participant Name_Video/Foto for the preliminary round, or Final SD_Gambar Ekspresi_Regency/City Name_Participant Name_Video/Foto for the final round. Upload to the participant's Google Drive with Anyone with the link can view, and enter the Google Drive or YouTube link in the application system.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Content must not carry SARA (ethnicity, religion, race and inter-group), pornography, provocative or political elements.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Weights: fit of the theme and story 10%; insight and knowledge about the chosen theme 20%; creativity (idea and handling of all visual aspects) 20%; aesthetic principles (composition, rhythm, depth or dimension, accent) 20%; skill in visual elements (shape, colour, line and plane) 20%; mastery of the drawing medium and tools 10%. Total 100%.\\n- The mark range printed in the guide is 100 to 1000."},{"Title":"Solo Singing (Menyanyi Solo)","Source":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab III B (pages 29-32)","Sections":{"About":["Solo singing is singing alone with good technique to interpret the song. It sharpens vocal skill and builds confidence, a big heart and sportsmanship."],"TimeAndFormat":["Preliminary round (online): every Juara 1 of a regency or city takes part. Each participant sings 1 Indonesian song and prepares the accompaniment. The song is one of: \\"Aku Indonesia\\" (Naura), \\"Ajaib\\" (Gempi), \\"Cinta untuk Mama\\" (Vidi Aldiano), \\"Perahu Laju Anganku Serta\\" (Maissy Pramaisshela), \\"Setinggi Langit\\" (Naura), \\"Hey\\" (Quinn Salman).","Final round (online): every province Juara 1 and every Indonesian School Overseas winner from the preliminary round takes part. Each participant sings 2 songs in 1 video. Song 1 is a national song with the participant's own accompaniment, one of: \\"Nyiur Hijau\\" (Maladi), \\"Berkibarlah Benderaku\\" (Ibu Sud), \\"Tanah Air\\" (Ibu Sud), \\"Indonesia Pusaka\\" (Ismail Marzuki). Song 2 is an Indonesian-language song from the same list of six used in the preliminary round.","Preliminary video: 1 singing video uploaded to the participant's Google Drive or YouTube. Maximum 5 minutes including the introduction, counted from the introduction until the song ends.","Final video: maximum 10 minutes for the 2 songs including the introduction. Both songs are recorded in 1 take.","In both rounds the video starts with the participant saying full name, date and day, school, city and province, category and the song. Then the participant starts singing at once, without a pause.","Video format is MP4, at least 720p."],"Rules":["Accompaniment can be MMO (music minus one, taken from YouTube or made by the participant) or an accompanist. The accompanist must not be seen in the video.","A microphone is optional, but the voice must be clear.","Costume is clothing with a touch of the participant's region, while staying modest and tasteful. The design must not limit movement and performance."],"Allowed":["Final round video must show a wall clock with moving hands and the singer in one frame, to prove the recording time."],"NotAllowed":["Final round: editing the picture or sound in any way."],"Judging":["Voice material (materi suara) 30%: pitch accuracy from start to end, quality of high and low notes, clarity and cleanness of the voice.","Vocal technique 30%: full use of vocal registers, breathing, articulation (pronunciation), rhythm that matches the accent of the song, start and end of the song.","Interpretation (penghayatan) 30%: feeling and understanding of the lyrics, and giving the message or story according to the meaning of the lyrics.","Appearance (penampilan) 10%: stage manner (confidence, contact with the audience, supporting movement), costume (fit to the song) and stage presence (charisma and attraction).","Mark scale for each indicator: 60 to 65 is Poor (kurang), 70 to 75 is Fair (cukup), 80 to 85 is Good (baik), 90 to 95 is Very Good (sangat baik)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo singing is singing alone with good technique to interpret the song. It sharpens vocal skill and builds confidence, a big heart and sportsmanship.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Preliminary round (online): every Juara 1 of a regency or city takes part. Each participant sings 1 Indonesian song and prepares the accompaniment. The song is one of: \\"Aku Indonesia\\" (Naura), \\"Ajaib\\" (Gempi), \\"Cinta untuk Mama\\" (Vidi Aldiano), \\"Perahu Laju Anganku Serta\\" (Maissy Pramaisshela), \\"Setinggi Langit\\" (Naura), \\"Hey\\" (Quinn Salman).\\n- Final round (online): every province Juara 1 and every Indonesian School Overseas winner from the preliminary round takes part. Each participant sings 2 songs in 1 video. Song 1 is a national song with the participant's own accompaniment, one of: \\"Nyiur Hijau\\" (Maladi), \\"Berkibarlah Benderaku\\" (Ibu Sud), \\"Tanah Air\\" (Ibu Sud), \\"Indonesia Pusaka\\" (Ismail Marzuki). Song 2 is an Indonesian-language song from the same list of six used in the preliminary round.\\n- Preliminary video: 1 singing video uploaded to the participant's Google Drive or YouTube. Maximum 5 minutes including the introduction, counted from the introduction until the song ends.\\n- Final video: maximum 10 minutes for the 2 songs including the introduction. Both songs are recorded in 1 take.\\n- In both rounds the video starts with the participant saying full name, date and day, school, city and province, category and the song. Then the participant starts singing at once, without a pause.\\n- Video format is MP4, at least 720p.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Accompaniment can be MMO (music minus one, taken from YouTube or made by the participant) or an accompanist. The accompanist must not be seen in the video.\\n- A microphone is optional, but the voice must be clear.\\n- Costume is clothing with a touch of the participant's region, while staying modest and tasteful. The design must not limit movement and performance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Final round video must show a wall clock with moving hands and the singer in one frame, to prove the recording time.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Final round: editing the picture or sound in any way.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Voice material (materi suara) 30%: pitch accuracy from start to end, quality of high and low notes, clarity and cleanness of the voice.\\n- Vocal technique 30%: full use of vocal registers, breathing, articulation (pronunciation), rhythm that matches the accent of the song, start and end of the song.\\n- Interpretation (penghayatan) 30%: feeling and understanding of the lyrics, and giving the message or story according to the meaning of the lyrics.\\n- Appearance (penampilan) 10%: stage manner (confidence, contact with the audience, supporting movement), costume (fit to the song) and stage presence (charisma and attraction).\\n- Mark scale for each indicator: 60 to 65 is Poor (kurang), 70 to 75 is Fair (cukup), 80 to 85 is Good (baik), 90 to 95 is Very Good (sangat baik)."},{"Title":"Craft from Plastic Bottle Waste (Kriya)","Source":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab III C (pages 33-40)","Sections":{"About":["Kriya is handmade craft art with its own character: craftsmanship, aesthetics, concept, function, form and style, made in limited numbers. The branch is a handicraft (prakarya) that uses waste materials, to train creativity, tradition and empathy.","Regional level theme: choose one of (1) a creative craft work, 2D aesthetic element, display or decoration, or (2) an innovative craft work, 3D, such as a toy, tool, aesthetic element, display or decoration.","National level theme: a creative 2D or 3D craft work with artistic innovation, which can be a toy, a functional product, or an aesthetic, decorative or display element."],"TimeAndFormat":["Medium: creations from used plastic bottles (mineral water, tea, juice, cooking oil bottles and so on). They may be combined with natural materials (wood, rattan, bamboo, fibres, leaves, stones, ceramics, leather) and industrial or factory-made materials (plastic rope, rubber sheet, foam, paper, cloth, styrofoam).","Size: a 2D or 3D work of about 50 cm x 50 cm up to a maximum of 100 cm x 100 cm (adjust to the child's body if a toy relates to a body function).","Materials and tools are provided by the participant. Tools can be cutters and saws, electric tools (drill, soldering iron, glue gun) and other tools such as brush, pencil, hammer and pliers.","The work is finished in a time that the participant manages, within the schedule set by the committee.","Preliminary round files: 5 photos of the work as PDF, 300 dpi, well lit: front, side, bottom, top, and a detail of a corner, edge or lock. A set can be shown in one photo.","Preliminary round video: a process video, maximum 5 minutes, MP4, showing the participant working. Visual flow: the whole gesture of the child mixed with close-ups of hands at work; the child's face in close-up; the prepared materials; the craft in progress from several angles; then back to the whole picture of the child working.","Files are uploaded to Google Drive (Anyone with the link can view), and the link is entered in the application system. Files are not uploaded directly to the application system.","A short description as a PDF (maximum one A4 page): form of the product, function, technique, name of the maker, regency or city, and province.","A scanned PDF of the originality statement.","Final round: the work is sent as photos and video in the same way as the preliminary round, with the originality statement. In the national round a participant may make a new work, or use the same or a modified provincial work, using modern and innovative methods and free techniques, without leaving traditional values."],"Rules":["Do not copy forms or works that already exist, such as craft products on the market or published on media.","The statement of originality says the work is the participant's own creativity, is not plagiarism or copying, and has not been entered in another competition. It is handed in when the work is collected.","The participant makes the work alone, without help, except certain techniques allowed for safety reasons.","The coach may not interfere artistically. The coach may only give technical help with tools that are unsafe for children and give moral support.","Visual content must not contain pornography or SARA (ethnicity, religion, race and inter-group).","A participant who is late to upload or send the work gets no extra time and is counted as out (gugur)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The jury judges by the visual look of the work, and the final mark is the average of the indicators.","Creativity and originality 25%: unique idea and visual concept, artistic innovation and newness, originality that marks the participant.","Technique and skill 25%: technical ability in handling and mastering the medium, clear creation of visual elements, control in execution and handling technical difficulty.","Form 20%: unique, proportional and aesthetic.","Presentation and fit to the theme 20%: neatness and finishing of the work, relevance to the theme.","Benefit (manfaat) 10%: fit to its use or function.","Each indicator is scored 1 to 10 (1-2 very poor, 3-5 poor, 6-8 good, 9-10 very good) and then taken to the weight above.","The jury may reduce marks if the work contains pornography or SARA, may disqualify a work that has entered another competition outside this programme, may reduce marks up to disqualification for any cheating in the work or the making of it, and the jury decision is final."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Kriya is handmade craft art with its own character: craftsmanship, aesthetics, concept, function, form and style, made in limited numbers. The branch is a handicraft (prakarya) that uses waste materials, to train creativity, tradition and empathy.\\n- Regional level theme: choose one of (1) a creative craft work, 2D aesthetic element, display or decoration, or (2) an innovative craft work, 3D, such as a toy, tool, aesthetic element, display or decoration.\\n- National level theme: a creative 2D or 3D craft work with artistic innovation, which can be a toy, a functional product, or an aesthetic, decorative or display element.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Medium: creations from used plastic bottles (mineral water, tea, juice, cooking oil bottles and so on). They may be combined with natural materials (wood, rattan, bamboo, fibres, leaves, stones, ceramics, leather) and industrial or factory-made materials (plastic rope, rubber sheet, foam, paper, cloth, styrofoam).\\n- Size: a 2D or 3D work of about 50 cm x 50 cm up to a maximum of 100 cm x 100 cm (adjust to the child's body if a toy relates to a body function).\\n- Materials and tools are provided by the participant. Tools can be cutters and saws, electric tools (drill, soldering iron, glue gun) and other tools such as brush, pencil, hammer and pliers.\\n- The work is finished in a time that the participant manages, within the schedule set by the committee.\\n- Preliminary round files: 5 photos of the work as PDF, 300 dpi, well lit: front, side, bottom, top, and a detail of a corner, edge or lock. A set can be shown in one photo.\\n- Preliminary round video: a process video, maximum 5 minutes, MP4, showing the participant working. Visual flow: the whole gesture of the child mixed with close-ups of hands at work; the child's face in close-up; the prepared materials; the craft in progress from several angles; then back to the whole picture of the child working.\\n- Files are uploaded to Google Drive (Anyone with the link can view), and the link is entered in the application system. Files are not uploaded directly to the application system.\\n- A short description as a PDF (maximum one A4 page): form of the product, function, technique, name of the maker, regency or city, and province.\\n- A scanned PDF of the originality statement.\\n- Final round: the work is sent as photos and video in the same way as the preliminary round, with the originality statement. In the national round a participant may make a new work, or use the same or a modified provincial work, using modern and innovative methods and free techniques, without leaving traditional values.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Do not copy forms or works that already exist, such as craft products on the market or published on media.\\n- The statement of originality says the work is the participant's own creativity, is not plagiarism or copying, and has not been entered in another competition. It is handed in when the work is collected.\\n- The participant makes the work alone, without help, except certain techniques allowed for safety reasons.\\n- The coach may not interfere artistically. The coach may only give technical help with tools that are unsafe for children and give moral support.\\n- Visual content must not contain pornography or SARA (ethnicity, religion, race and inter-group).\\n- A participant who is late to upload or send the work gets no extra time and is counted as out (gugur).\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The jury judges by the visual look of the work, and the final mark is the average of the indicators.\\n- Creativity and originality 25%: unique idea and visual concept, artistic innovation and newness, originality that marks the participant.\\n- Technique and skill 25%: technical ability in handling and mastering the medium, clear creation of visual elements, control in execution and handling technical difficulty.\\n- Form 20%: unique, proportional and aesthetic.\\n- Presentation and fit to the theme 20%: neatness and finishing of the work, relevance to the theme.\\n- Benefit (manfaat) 10%: fit to its use or function.\\n- Each indicator is scored 1 to 10 (1-2 very poor, 3-5 poor, 6-8 good, 9-10 very good) and then taken to the weight above.\\n- The jury may reduce marks if the work contains pornography or SARA, may disqualify a work that has entered another competition outside this programme, may reduce marks up to disqualification for any cheating in the work or the making of it, and the jury decision is final."},{"Title":"Storytelling (Mendongeng)","Source":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab III D (pages 41-46)","Sections":{"About":["The storytelling competition is oral storytelling by one participant, without reading a text or script. The story is fiction, from a children's story book or a work of the participant, teacher, trainer or coach.","Stages: school level (a school registers at most 2 participants for the regency or city selection); regency or city level (online or offline, to choose 1 best participant per regency or city); national level with a preliminary round (online, 1 best participant per province) and a final round (online, 6 best participants as Juara 1, 2, 3 and Harapan 1, 2, 3)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Video length is 5 to 10 minutes: at most 2 minutes for the introduction and opening sentence, and at most 8 minutes for the storytelling. The correct length is one of the judged factors.","The video is audio visual in 16:9 landscape, MP4, at least 720p.","A participant sends only 1 storytelling video, used for the regency or city selection (where it is online) and the national preliminary round.","A participant who reaches the national final must make a new storytelling video. A finalist may not reuse the story from the preliminary round.","The video is sent through the FLS3N SD application system."],"Rules":["The special theme is the Seven Habits of Great Indonesian Children (wake up early, worship, exercise, eat healthy, love learning, take part in society, sleep early). A participant can choose one or more of them for the story.","The script can be adapted from fairy tale books, legends, folk stories and fables from Indonesia. An original story (idea and text written by the participant) is a plus.","Use good, simple Indonesian that is easy to understand. A regional-language word, term or sentence is allowed if the Indonesian meaning is told right after it. Regional language is not used for the whole story.","The story reflects the characteristics of SD/MI students and brings up local culture.","The story has been edited for violence, killing, power struggles, romance, excessive romanticism and infidelity, without losing the essence of the adapted story.","No conclusion or moral message is needed in the story or at the end.","Participants are advised to say the title of the book or source, the author and illustrator (if any), at the start or end of the story.","Wear a school uniform without make-up. Costume ornaments in harmony with the story are allowed in the preliminary and final rounds.","Props are allowed but not required. Props only support the story and are not stage decoration.","Other skills such as dance, singing or playing an instrument are allowed if they match the story, but not required. Avoid heavy equipment or large space for them."],"Allowed":["Recording with a phone or camera in a static position (no movement, no change of focus) from one front angle.","A video that is one whole, recorded in one take."],"NotAllowed":["Editing the video (cutting, joining or adding).","Adding music, extra sound, extra video or pictures, or graphics."],"Judging":["Story interpretation 30%: story content fits the contest theme; command of the story (flow, characters, educational message) shown in intonation, volume and tempo; use of expression, body language and movement that suit the story.","Storytelling presentation 40%: confidence (eye contact, body language, telling the story without memorising it word for word); good, simple and clear Indonesian; vocal clarity (articulation); command of the stage and interaction.","Creativity 30%: an original story; use of props, body language and other skills such as singing and dancing; improvisation in telling the story; costume ornament that fits the story.","Each indicator is scored by how many sub-indicators are met (4 met is 90, 3 is 80, 2 is 70, 1 is 60). The mark intervals are 60 to 65 Poor, 70 to 75 Fair, 80 to 85 Good, 90 to 100 Very Good."],"Points":null,"Notes":["The guide's heading for the storytelling theme says SMP/MTs, but the text is for the primary school level."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The storytelling competition is oral storytelling by one participant, without reading a text or script. The story is fiction, from a children's story book or a work of the participant, teacher, trainer or coach.\\n- Stages: school level (a school registers at most 2 participants for the regency or city selection); regency or city level (online or offline, to choose 1 best participant per regency or city); national level with a preliminary round (online, 1 best participant per province) and a final round (online, 6 best participants as Juara 1, 2, 3 and Harapan 1, 2, 3).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Video length is 5 to 10 minutes: at most 2 minutes for the introduction and opening sentence, and at most 8 minutes for the storytelling. The correct length is one of the judged factors.\\n- The video is audio visual in 16:9 landscape, MP4, at least 720p.\\n- A participant sends only 1 storytelling video, used for the regency or city selection (where it is online) and the national preliminary round.\\n- A participant who reaches the national final must make a new storytelling video. A finalist may not reuse the story from the preliminary round.\\n- The video is sent through the FLS3N SD application system.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The special theme is the Seven Habits of Great Indonesian Children (wake up early, worship, exercise, eat healthy, love learning, take part in society, sleep early). A participant can choose one or more of them for the story.\\n- The script can be adapted from fairy tale books, legends, folk stories and fables from Indonesia. An original story (idea and text written by the participant) is a plus.\\n- Use good, simple Indonesian that is easy to understand. A regional-language word, term or sentence is allowed if the Indonesian meaning is told right after it. Regional language is not used for the whole story.\\n- The story reflects the characteristics of SD/MI students and brings up local culture.\\n- The story has been edited for violence, killing, power struggles, romance, excessive romanticism and infidelity, without losing the essence of the adapted story.\\n- No conclusion or moral message is needed in the story or at the end.\\n- Participants are advised to say the title of the book or source, the author and illustrator (if any), at the start or end of the story.\\n- Wear a school uniform without make-up. Costume ornaments in harmony with the story are allowed in the preliminary and final rounds.\\n- Props are allowed but not required. Props only support the story and are not stage decoration.\\n- Other skills such as dance, singing or playing an instrument are allowed if they match the story, but not required. Avoid heavy equipment or large space for them.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Recording with a phone or camera in a static position (no movement, no change of focus) from one front angle.\\n- A video that is one whole, recorded in one take.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Editing the video (cutting, joining or adding).\\n- Adding music, extra sound, extra video or pictures, or graphics.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Story interpretation 30%: story content fits the contest theme; command of the story (flow, characters, educational message) shown in intonation, volume and tempo; use of expression, body language and movement that suit the story.\\n- Storytelling presentation 40%: confidence (eye contact, body language, telling the story without memorising it word for word); good, simple and clear Indonesian; vocal clarity (articulation); command of the stage and interaction.\\n- Creativity 30%: an original story; use of props, body language and other skills such as singing and dancing; improvisation in telling the story; costume ornament that fits the story.\\n- Each indicator is scored by how many sub-indicators are met (4 met is 90, 3 is 80, 2 is 70, 1 is 60). The mark intervals are 60 to 65 Poor, 70 to 75 Fair, 80 to 85 Good, 90 to 100 Very Good.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The guide's heading for the storytelling theme says SMP/MTs, but the text is for the primary school level."},{"Title":"Story Writing (Menulis Cerita)","Source":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab III E (pages 47-51)","Sections":{"About":["The story writing competition is a contest between students to put ideas into a written fiction story, in a creative and interesting way. The story has theme, characters, plot, setting and language style. Sources can be imagination, references, observation, and personal or other people's experience.","Stages: regency or city level, set by each regency or city following this guide, and national level with a preliminary round (best work of each province) and a final round (national champion)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Preliminary round: choose one theme: (a) building seven good habits (wake up early, worship, exercise, eat healthy and nutritious food, love learning, take part in society, sleep early); (b) {{StoryThemeEarth}}; (c) {{StoryThemeAdventure}}.","Preliminary format: Calibri font size 12, 1.5 line spacing, A4 paper, 2.54 cm margins on each side, story length 500 to 1,700 words.","The manuscript carries: branch, story title, full name of the participant, school name, regency or city, province. The genre is free.","Upload the work to the participant's Google Drive with Anyone with the link can view. Name the file Participant Name_Branch_School Name. Enter the Google Drive link in the application system in the set format.","Upload the Statement of Originality with a Rp10,000 stamp, signed by the participant.","The national preliminary jury judges all works and picks 1 best work from each province for the final.","Final round: online, at the same time for everybody, at a time set by the committee. It is 4 hours long.","Before the final there is an online technical meeting where the rules, the work rules and the way to send the work are read. The schedule is announced by an announcement letter on the Pusat Prestasi Nasional website and Instagram.","The story theme of the final is announced just before the contest.","Each participant writes live in Google Docs on an electronic device (laptop, tablet, notebook or smartphone).","The manuscript carries the story title, full name, school and province.","A participant can hand in the work before time is up. The work must be sent before the deadline by the email address provided, with the file name Participant Name_School_Province.","The work is judged by the jury team. The jury can validate a work by interviewing the participant when needed."],"Rules":["The story is in good Indonesian.","The story is the participant's own original work, shown by a signed statement of originality on a Rp10,000 stamp.","The story must not be made with AI (artificial intelligence).","The story has not been published in any media.","The content has no discrimination against ethnicity, religion, race or a group, and no violence, hate speech or pornography.","The work needs no explicit conclusion, moral message, cover illustration or content illustration.","Final round: the participant writes indoors and gets no help from other people.","Final round: the participant must use two devices. The first is for writing. The second logs in to the Zoom meeting under the name School Name_Participant Name, with its camera on and pointed at the participant's work desk (the guide shows an example camera angle).","Final round: the participant may ask the companion for help with a technical problem such as lost signal or a dead device.","Final round: the participant may open a search engine, books and dictionary to support the writing, but must not use chat applications or AI.","Final round: the participant must not chat with the companion or other people in a way that helps the writing.","Final round: the committee provides a facilitator for technical questions. Talk to the facilitator through the Zoom chat so other participants are not disturbed.","Final round: to leave the room, ask the facilitator by Zoom chat first.","Final round: the jury and facilitators watch the writing to check honesty, and can ask the participant at any time to show the room, the screen and so on."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Authenticity of the story idea 35%: the uniqueness of the story idea.","Creativity in handling the story 25%: ability to turn the theme into an attractive and memorable story.","Use of Indonesian 20%: fit of the language as a medium of expression, including word choice, sentence structure, spelling and punctuation.","Message 20%: ability to give a moving message from the story.","Mark intervals for each indicator: 60 to 65 Poor (against the rules, unfinished, or below basic standard), 70 to 75 Fair (good in some aspects, weak in others), 80 to 85 Good (good overall with some flaws), 90 to 95 Very Good (good in every aspect, nearly perfect).","A participant who is proved to plagiarise, send work that is not purely their own or made with AI, or cheat in another way, is disqualified now or later, is banned from similar contests in the future, and any prize, award or title already received is revoked and must be returned.","Minor breaches of the technical rules for writing and sending the work mean a reduced mark and/or disqualification."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The story writing competition is a contest between students to put ideas into a written fiction story, in a creative and interesting way. The story has theme, characters, plot, setting and language style. Sources can be imagination, references, observation, and personal or other people's experience.\\n- Stages: regency or city level, set by each regency or city following this guide, and national level with a preliminary round (best work of each province) and a final round (national champion).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Preliminary round: choose one theme: (a) building seven good habits (wake up early, worship, exercise, eat healthy and nutritious food, love learning, take part in society, sleep early); (b) {{StoryThemeEarth}}; (c) {{StoryThemeAdventure}}.\\n- Preliminary format: Calibri font size 12, 1.5 line spacing, A4 paper, 2.54 cm margins on each side, story length 500 to 1,700 words.\\n- The manuscript carries: branch, story title, full name of the participant, school name, regency or city, province. The genre is free.\\n- Upload the work to the participant's Google Drive with Anyone with the link can view. Name the file Participant Name_Branch_School Name. Enter the Google Drive link in the application system in the set format.\\n- Upload the Statement of Originality with a Rp10,000 stamp, signed by the participant.\\n- The national preliminary jury judges all works and picks 1 best work from each province for the final.\\n- Final round: online, at the same time for everybody, at a time set by the committee. It is 4 hours long.\\n- Before the final there is an online technical meeting where the rules, the work rules and the way to send the work are read. The schedule is announced by an announcement letter on the Pusat Prestasi Nasional website and Instagram.\\n- The story theme of the final is announced just before the contest.\\n- Each participant writes live in Google Docs on an electronic device (laptop, tablet, notebook or smartphone).\\n- The manuscript carries the story title, full name, school and province.\\n- A participant can hand in the work before time is up. The work must be sent before the deadline by the email address provided, with the file name Participant Name_School_Province.\\n- The work is judged by the jury team. The jury can validate a work by interviewing the participant when needed.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The story is in good Indonesian.\\n- The story is the participant's own original work, shown by a signed statement of originality on a Rp10,000 stamp.\\n- The story must not be made with AI (artificial intelligence).\\n- The story has not been published in any media.\\n- The content has no discrimination against ethnicity, religion, race or a group, and no violence, hate speech or pornography.\\n- The work needs no explicit conclusion, moral message, cover illustration or content illustration.\\n- Final round: the participant writes indoors and gets no help from other people.\\n- Final round: the participant must use two devices. The first is for writing. The second logs in to the Zoom meeting under the name School Name_Participant Name, with its camera on and pointed at the participant's work desk (the guide shows an example camera angle).\\n- Final round: the participant may ask the companion for help with a technical problem such as lost signal or a dead device.\\n- Final round: the participant may open a search engine, books and dictionary to support the writing, but must not use chat applications or AI.\\n- Final round: the participant must not chat with the companion or other people in a way that helps the writing.\\n- Final round: the committee provides a facilitator for technical questions. Talk to the facilitator through the Zoom chat so other participants are not disturbed.\\n- Final round: to leave the room, ask the facilitator by Zoom chat first.\\n- Final round: the jury and facilitators watch the writing to check honesty, and can ask the participant at any time to show the room, the screen and so on.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Authenticity of the story idea 35%: the uniqueness of the story idea.\\n- Creativity in handling the story 25%: ability to turn the theme into an attractive and memorable story.\\n- Use of Indonesian 20%: fit of the language as a medium of expression, including word choice, sentence structure, spelling and punctuation.\\n- Message 20%: ability to give a moving message from the story.\\n- Mark intervals for each indicator: 60 to 65 Poor (against the rules, unfinished, or below basic standard), 70 to 75 Fair (good in some aspects, weak in others), 80 to 85 Good (good overall with some flaws), 90 to 95 Very Good (good in every aspect, nearly perfect).\\n- A participant who is proved to plagiarise, send work that is not purely their own or made with AI, or cheat in another way, is disqualified now or later, is banned from similar contests in the future, and any prize, award or title already received is revoked and must be returned.\\n- Minor breaches of the technical rules for writing and sending the work mean a reduced mark and/or disqualification."},{"Title":"Pantomime (Pantomim)","Source":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab III F (pages 52-57)","Sections":{"About":["Pantomime is an imaginative performing art that shows an object or thing with body movement and facial expression to give a feeling and message. The competition stresses non-verbal communication, creativity, character growth, movement (motor and sensory skill of the child) and expression with local content and good cultural values.","Pantomime is an art of silence. It trains active listening, focus, respect, tolerance and patience, and it develops the eight multiple intelligences of Howard Gardner.","Aims: to build character and mentality (capable, sporting and creative); to sharpen imagination, focus, creativity and confidence; to improve motor skill through healthy, supple body technique; to grow empathy for the surroundings; and to give a place for talent and interest in pantomime at national and international level."],"TimeAndFormat":["Regency or city level: the performance is online or offline as each Education Office decides, following this guide. Length is about 6 minutes including the presentation of the work. Length does not affect the mark.","Regency or city level: hand the story synopsis and the music in mp3 format on a flash drive to the regency or city committee. Stage orientation is used to get to know and master the stage.","National preliminary round (online): Juara 1 of the regency or city of 38 provinces. Send an MP4 video, at least 720p, about 6 minutes including the presentation of the work. Sound must be clear. The video must be bright and clear so the expression and body movement can be seen. The video matches the theme. Length does not affect the mark.","National final (online): Juara 1 of each province from the preliminary round. Send an MP4 video, at least 720p, with the same theme as the preliminary round. The participants may develop and maximise the work. About 8 minutes including the presentation of the work. Sound must be clear and the video must be bright and clear. Length does not affect the mark.","Theme at national level: {{PantomimeTheme}}. It means helping others in need willingly, with money, effort, ideas, or support through good advice or example.","The synopsis of the work is uploaded to the application system as PDF or DOCX, named Pantomime Title_School Name_Province."],"Rules":["The group is 2 participants. They can be male, female or mixed.","The work must follow the material rules set.","Pantomime costume and make-up are provided by the participants.","The participants must make their own accompaniment music and avoid copyrighted music of other people.","BPTI prepares accompaniment music with several rhythms that participants may use. The participants may choose, mix, edit and add sound effects as they like.","The work is rooted in Indonesian culture and does not offend PARAS (pornography, religion, race, inter-group and ethnicity).","Final round: the costume has regional elements.","The participants must present the pantomime work (introduce themselves and tell a little of the synopsis).","The jury can reduce marks, lower the rank and/or disqualify participants who do not follow the rules. The decision of the jury is final."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Any props.","Plagiarism: a work that already exists on YouTube or other media, or is similar to a work of someone else that can be detected.","Content that offends pornography, religion, race, inter-group or ethnicity (PARAS).","Detected use of copyrighted music of other people."],"Judging":["Concept 20%: creativity, power of imagination, fit to the theme; how the idea and story are built and the show is designed from start to end, including consistency with the imaginary object, cause and effect between scenes, and the characters created.","Movement 30%: body technique, flexibility and harmony; variety of movements, flexibility and balance in beautiful movement, synchronisation of movement with the timing of the music, and togetherness of movement on stage.","Expression 30%: facial expression and feeling (penjiwaan); entering the role and the changes when different emotions appear in the story.","Marks are reduced when the participants show no facial expression or use excessive make-up.","Insight (wawasan) 20%: attitude and appearance (costume and face make-up), togetherness and knowledge; seen when the participants introduce themselves, tell a little of the synopsis, and in the design of make-up and costume, neatness, cleanliness and attraction.","Mark scale for each indicator: 60 to 65 is Poor (kurang), 70 to 75 is Fair (cukup), 80 to 85 is Good (baik), 90 to 95 is Very Good (sangat baik)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Pantomime is an imaginative performing art that shows an object or thing with body movement and facial expression to give a feeling and message. The competition stresses non-verbal communication, creativity, character growth, movement (motor and sensory skill of the child) and expression with local content and good cultural values.\\n- Pantomime is an art of silence. It trains active listening, focus, respect, tolerance and patience, and it develops the eight multiple intelligences of Howard Gardner.\\n- Aims: to build character and mentality (capable, sporting and creative); to sharpen imagination, focus, creativity and confidence; to improve motor skill through healthy, supple body technique; to grow empathy for the surroundings; and to give a place for talent and interest in pantomime at national and international level.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Regency or city level: the performance is online or offline as each Education Office decides, following this guide. Length is about 6 minutes including the presentation of the work. Length does not affect the mark.\\n- Regency or city level: hand the story synopsis and the music in mp3 format on a flash drive to the regency or city committee. Stage orientation is used to get to know and master the stage.\\n- National preliminary round (online): Juara 1 of the regency or city of 38 provinces. Send an MP4 video, at least 720p, about 6 minutes including the presentation of the work. Sound must be clear. The video must be bright and clear so the expression and body movement can be seen. The video matches the theme. Length does not affect the mark.\\n- National final (online): Juara 1 of each province from the preliminary round. Send an MP4 video, at least 720p, with the same theme as the preliminary round. The participants may develop and maximise the work. About 8 minutes including the presentation of the work. Sound must be clear and the video must be bright and clear. Length does not affect the mark.\\n- Theme at national level: {{PantomimeTheme}}. It means helping others in need willingly, with money, effort, ideas, or support through good advice or example.\\n- The synopsis of the work is uploaded to the application system as PDF or DOCX, named Pantomime Title_School Name_Province.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The group is 2 participants. They can be male, female or mixed.\\n- The work must follow the material rules set.\\n- Pantomime costume and make-up are provided by the participants.\\n- The participants must make their own accompaniment music and avoid copyrighted music of other people.\\n- BPTI prepares accompaniment music with several rhythms that participants may use. The participants may choose, mix, edit and add sound effects as they like.\\n- The work is rooted in Indonesian culture and does not offend PARAS (pornography, religion, race, inter-group and ethnicity).\\n- Final round: the costume has regional elements.\\n- The participants must present the pantomime work (introduce themselves and tell a little of the synopsis).\\n- The jury can reduce marks, lower the rank and/or disqualify participants who do not follow the rules. The decision of the jury is final.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Any props.\\n- Plagiarism: a work that already exists on YouTube or other media, or is similar to a work of someone else that can be detected.\\n- Content that offends pornography, religion, race, inter-group or ethnicity (PARAS).\\n- Detected use of copyrighted music of other people.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Concept 20%: creativity, power of imagination, fit to the theme; how the idea and story are built and the show is designed from start to end, including consistency with the imaginary object, cause and effect between scenes, and the characters created.\\n- Movement 30%: body technique, flexibility and harmony; variety of movements, flexibility and balance in beautiful movement, synchronisation of movement with the timing of the music, and togetherness of movement on stage.\\n- Expression 30%: facial expression and feeling (penjiwaan); entering the role and the changes when different emotions appear in the story.\\n- Marks are reduced when the participants show no facial expression or use excessive make-up.\\n- Insight (wawasan) 20%: attitude and appearance (costume and face make-up), togetherness and knowledge; seen when the participants introduce themselves, tell a little of the synopsis, and in the design of make-up and costume, neatness, cleanliness and attraction.\\n- Mark scale for each indicator: 60 to 65 is Poor (kurang), 70 to 75 is Fair (cukup), 80 to 85 is Good (baik), 90 to 95 is Very Good (sangat baik)."},{"Title":"Dance (Tari)","Source":"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab III G (pages 58-62)","Sections":{"About":["Dance is an art of expression by well-organised body movement. Dance movement is not daily movement. It expresses feeling with meaning that the audience can enjoy and feel.","In FLS3N primary level, dance works are new creations suited to the age and psychology of children. The student works with a choreographer, trainer or teacher on a theme and the body's response to it, matching the child's understanding.","Aims: to introduce new creative dance based on local content; to develop the child's personality (moral, culture and customs); to build confidence; to develop creativity in the dance elements wiraga, wirama, wirasa and wirupa; and to grow human values."],"TimeAndFormat":["The dance work lasts 5 to 7 minutes.","Regional theme: ideas from the daily life of the child in the social and cultural environment and tradition. The technique is movement with handling of space, time and energy suited to the theme. The performance uses make-up, costume and stage space effectively. Creativity means newness and innovation in movement, music and suitability to the child's development.","Regional video: recorded indoors in a room of a size the work needs, or outdoors if it supports the choreography. The camera is in front and static. Enough distance between dancers and camera shows the whole work from start to end. Resolution is 750p (as printed). The title, synopsis and dancers' names show at the start of the video, not counted in the 5 to 7 minutes.","National stage (online): the same work as at regional level. Participants may improve the work and send a video to the FLS3N 2025 committee link to be shown in the final. If the video is recorded again, the camera is in front and static, and the distance shows the whole work.","Hand in a synopsis explaining the concept as a PDF by the time set: (1) title, (2) theme, (3) choreographer, music arranger and costume designer, (4) names of the supporting people."],"Rules":["The group is 3 to 5 performers.","Prepare one new dance work.","The work is rooted in the local culture of the participants.","The movement is based on Indonesian traditional dance movement that has been developed creatively to fit the theme.","Accompaniment music is a recording in MP3. It is not cut from existing dance works, shows traditional music elements of the local area, and may mix in modern instruments.","Costume, make-up and other support are prepared by the participants and fit the theme and the age of the participants.","The work must be a purely new work that has never been staged.","The work must not exceed the set length."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Props with sharp objects, unless the prop is an imitation and safe to support the work.","Content with SARA (ethnicity, religion, race and inter-group), pornography, provocative or political elements.","Using existing dance music."],"Judging":["Judging is a curation process: identify, judge, conclude and give a quality and suitability standard to the dance work.","Idea (15): originality of idea; movement developed from traditional or non-traditional dance types; sources such as folk tales, legends, myths, hikayat, play and games.","Technique (25): mastery of movement technique, handling of space, handling of time, handling of energy.","Performance (30): expression, make-up, costume, handling of the stage space, harmony, use of props.","Creativity (30): newness, innovation, suitability to the child's development, accompaniment music.","Total weight is 100%."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Dance is an art of expression by well-organised body movement. Dance movement is not daily movement. It expresses feeling with meaning that the audience can enjoy and feel.\\n- In FLS3N primary level, dance works are new creations suited to the age and psychology of children. The student works with a choreographer, trainer or teacher on a theme and the body's response to it, matching the child's understanding.\\n- Aims: to introduce new creative dance based on local content; to develop the child's personality (moral, culture and customs); to build confidence; to develop creativity in the dance elements wiraga, wirama, wirasa and wirupa; and to grow human values.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The dance work lasts 5 to 7 minutes.\\n- Regional theme: ideas from the daily life of the child in the social and cultural environment and tradition. The technique is movement with handling of space, time and energy suited to the theme. The performance uses make-up, costume and stage space effectively. Creativity means newness and innovation in movement, music and suitability to the child's development.\\n- Regional video: recorded indoors in a room of a size the work needs, or outdoors if it supports the choreography. The camera is in front and static. Enough distance between dancers and camera shows the whole work from start to end. Resolution is 750p (as printed). The title, synopsis and dancers' names show at the start of the video, not counted in the 5 to 7 minutes.\\n- National stage (online): the same work as at regional level. Participants may improve the work and send a video to the FLS3N 2025 committee link to be shown in the final. If the video is recorded again, the camera is in front and static, and the distance shows the whole work.\\n- Hand in a synopsis explaining the concept as a PDF by the time set: (1) title, (2) theme, (3) choreographer, music arranger and costume designer, (4) names of the supporting people.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The group is 3 to 5 performers.\\n- Prepare one new dance work.\\n- The work is rooted in the local culture of the participants.\\n- The movement is based on Indonesian traditional dance movement that has been developed creatively to fit the theme.\\n- Accompaniment music is a recording in MP3. It is not cut from existing dance works, shows traditional music elements of the local area, and may mix in modern instruments.\\n- Costume, make-up and other support are prepared by the participants and fit the theme and the age of the participants.\\n- The work must be a purely new work that has never been staged.\\n- The work must not exceed the set length.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Props with sharp objects, unless the prop is an imitation and safe to support the work.\\n- Content with SARA (ethnicity, religion, race and inter-group), pornography, provocative or political elements.\\n- Using existing dance music.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is a curation process: identify, judge, conclude and give a quality and suitability standard to the dance work.\\n- Idea (15): originality of idea; movement developed from traditional or non-traditional dance types; sources such as folk tales, legends, myths, hikayat, play and games.\\n- Technique (25): mastery of movement technique, handling of space, handling of time, handling of energy.\\n- Performance (30): expression, make-up, costume, handling of the stage space, harmony, use of props.\\n- Creativity (30): newness, innovation, suitability to the child's development, accompaniment music.\\n- Total weight is 100%."}]`),r=[],s=[{Key:"GeneralTheme",Kind:"text",Label:"General theme",Value:"Ekspresi Seni, Inspirasi Negeri (Artistic Expression, Inspiration of the Nation)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab I F"},{Key:"SpecialTheme",Kind:"text",Label:"Special theme",Value:"Tujuh Kebiasaan Anak Indonesia Hebat (Seven Habits of Great Indonesian Children)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab I F"},{Key:"DrawingPreliminaryTheme",Kind:"text",Label:"Expressive Drawing preliminary theme",Value:"Ayo Sayangi Keluargamu! (Let's Love Your Family!)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.24"},{Key:"DrawingFinalTheme",Kind:"text",Label:"Expressive Drawing final theme",Value:"Olahraga itu Sehat! (Sport Is Healthy!)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.26"},{Key:"StoryThemeEarth",Kind:"text",Label:"Story Writing theme 2",Value:"Bumi yang asyik (A fun earth)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.47"},{Key:"StoryThemeAdventure",Kind:"text",Label:"Story Writing theme 3",Value:"Petualangan tak terlupakan (An unforgettable adventure)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.47"},{Key:"PantomimeTheme",Kind:"text",Label:"Pantomime national theme",Value:"Berderma (Giving to those in need)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.55"},{Key:"Socialisation",Kind:"date",Label:"Introduction of FLS3N Dikdas 2025",Value:"Third week of April 2025 (schedule announced on Instagram @puspresnas)",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.17 schedule 1"},{Key:"RegistrationOpen",Kind:"date",Label:"School registration opens",Value:"2025-03-28",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.17 schedule 2"},{Key:"RegistrationClose",Kind:"date",Label:"School registration closes (23:59 WIB)",Value:"2025-05-10",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.17 schedule 3"},{Key:"DistrictNotice",Kind:"date",Label:"Registration data sent to regency or city Education Offices",Value:"2025-05-15",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.17 schedule 4"},{Key:"DistrictRoundDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Regency or city level period",Value:"18 May to 14 July 2025",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.17 schedule 5"},{Key:"DistrictRoundDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for regency or city uploads (23:59 WIB)",Value:"2025-07-14",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.17 schedule 6"},{Key:"PreliminaryAnnouncement",Kind:"date",Label:"National preliminary round participants announced",Value:"2025-07-21",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.17 schedule 7"},{Key:"PreliminaryJudging",Kind:"date",Label:"National preliminary round judging",Value:"22 July to 1 August 2025",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.18 schedule 8"},{Key:"PreliminaryResults",Kind:"date",Label:"Preliminary results, province winners and National Finalists published",Value:"2025-08-03",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.18 schedule 9"},{Key:"FinalUploadWindow",Kind:"date",Label:"National Finalists upload their work (until 23:59 WIB)",Value:"4 to 18 August 2025",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.18 schedule 10"},{Key:"NationalFinalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"National final (online)",Value:"15 to 20 September 2025",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.18 schedule 11"},{Key:"WinnersAnnounced",Kind:"date",Label:"National winners announced",Value:"2025-09-23",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, p.18 schedule 12"},{Key:"StampFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Stamp on each statement letter",Value:"Rp10,000 stamp (meterai tempel) on each of the two statement letters",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab II B 9"},{Key:"RegistrationPortal",Kind:"link",Label:"Participant registration portal",Value:"https://daftar-bpti.kemdikbud.go.id",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab II F 1"},{Key:"EventApp",Kind:"link",Label:"FLS3N SD/MI application system",Value:"https://sd.pusatprestasinasional.kemdikbud.go.id/lomba/session/index?jl=fls2n",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab II F 2"},{Key:"InfoSites",Kind:"link",Label:"Information sites of the festival",Value:"https://pusatprestasinasional.kemdikbud.go.id/ and https://bpti.kemdikbud.go.id/ and Instagram @puspresnas",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab II F 3"},{Key:"CertificateSite",Kind:"link",Label:"E-certificate download",Value:"https://esertifikat.pusatprestasinasional.kemdikbud.go.id/",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025, Bab II F 4"}],l=[{Claim:"Eligibility, selection levels, upload rules, schedule, awards, conduct rules and all seven branch rules and criteria written here come from the Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025 (March 2025), pages 1 to 64 and the two appendix letters.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025",Url:"https://pusatprestasinasional.kemdikbud.go.id/uploads/lampiran/Panduan%20Teknis%20Pelaksanaan%20FLS3N%20SD%202025.pdf"},{Claim:"The guide prints no entry fee, no phone number or email contact for participants, no venue (the national rounds are online) and no news items. Nothing was written from general knowledge.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Panduan Teknis Pelaksanaan FLS3N SD 2025",Url:"https://pusatprestasinasional.kemdikbud.go.id/uploads/lampiran/Panduan%20Teknis%20Pelaksanaan%20FLS3N%20SD%202025.pdf"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:a,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,a as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,h as Year,c as default};
